# Spec sources (public sources/ + private capture-log)

SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later

Whenever a file under `tavera/specs/<component>/` cites guest, probe, or
debugging evidence, keep **two** durable copies and make the **public** one
the citation target.

`<component>` matches `tavera/specs/<component>/` (for example
`amd64-logical-processors`, `ntfs`).

## Public evidence folder (cited)

```text
tavera/specs/<component>/sources/
```

This folder is committed with the public tree. It holds **only** evidence
files the specs or debugging log actually reference: guest/probe logs from
`output/`, related probe capture artifacts, and debugging-session logs.
It does **not** hold Microsoft Learn / OpenSpecs PDFs, scraped web text, or
unrelated build products (ISOs, `.exe`, disk images, firmware vars).

Public Spec Sources, open-item resolutions, and `debugging-YYYY-MM-DD.md`
cite paths under `tavera/specs/<component>/sources/…` (plus the probe under
`tavera/probes/…` when applicable), with the marker (`DIFF END OK`, etc.).
Do **not** cite raw `output/…` once the file has been copied here.

Layout under the public folder:

```text
tavera/specs/<component>/sources/
  README.md                      # optional; what belongs here
  probes/<probe-id>/…            # Spec Sources guest / probe logs
  debugging-YYYY-MM-DD/…         # evidence for that debugging log
```

Prefer the same basenames as under `output/`. Keep a short `README.md` that
says these files are cited evidence, not Learn PDFs.

## Private archive (also required; never named in public docs)

Also copy every cited evidence file into the **private** project-root
capture tree (sibling of `source/`, not committed to the public repo):

```text
capture-log/sources/spec/<component>/
```

Mirror the same relative layout (`probes/…`, `debugging-YYYY-MM-DD/…`).
Refresh the private copy whenever the public `sources/` copy is refreshed.

This private tree also holds kinds that must **not** enter `tavera/specs/`:

```text
capture-log/sources/spec/<component>/
  README.md
  manifest.md
  web/                         # printed PDFs of cited Learn / OpenSpecs pages
  intree/                      # excerpts from this checkout
  probes/                      # mirror of public guest / probe logs
  other/                       # this project's GitHub milestone JSON, etc.
  debugging-YYYY-MM-DD/        # mirror of public debugging evidence
```

Never name `capture-log`, `capture-log/sources`, or “private archive” in
`tavera/specs/`, public README text under `tavera/`, or other public docs
that describe Sources. Agents keep the private tree; public citations name
Learn/`https://` URLs, in-tree paths, `tavera/specs/<component>/sources/…`,
`tavera/probes/…`, or this project’s GitHub URLs.

Every artifact in either tree must have a matching public citation. Do not
leave an orphan log or PDF with no Spec Sources / debugging / open-item
reference.

## What to store where

| Kind | Public `tavera/specs/…/sources/` | Private `capture-log/sources/spec/…/` |
|------|----------------------------------|----------------------------------------|
| Guest / probe log | Yes — copy from `output/`; **cite this path** | Yes — same file mirrored |
| Debugging-session log | Yes — under `debugging-YYYY-MM-DD/` | Yes — mirrored |
| Learn / OpenSpecs page | No | Yes — print to PDF + `.meta.txt` |
| In-tree excerpt | No (cite the live in-tree path) | Yes — short excerpt with commit SHA and start lines |
| GitHub milestone / issue | No (cite the GitHub URL) | Yes — JSON/markdown from `gh` optional |

When the run finishes (or in the same turn as the citation), copy from
`output/` into the public `sources/` path **and** into the private mirror.
If `output/` is already gone but the public `sources/` copy exists, refresh
the private mirror from that public copy.

Keep artifacts small enough to prove the citation. Do not paste log bodies
into the markdown spec ([specs.mdc](specs.mdc)).

## Citation examples

```text
Right: tavera/specs/amd64-logical-processors/sources/probes/probe-v1/windows-4c1t.log (DIFF END OK); probe tavera/probes/…
Right: debugging log cites tavera/specs/…/sources/debugging-2026-11-18/boot-m32-….log
Right: [GetLogicalProcessorInformationEx](https://learn.microsoft.com/…). …
Right: sdk/include/xdk/ketypes.h in this tree. …
Wrong: citing only output/… after the file was copied into sources/
Wrong: citing capture-log/… in tavera/specs/
Wrong: storing Learn PDFs under tavera/specs/…/sources/
Wrong: a log under sources/ with no matching public citation
Wrong: public sources/ copy without a private capture-log mirror (or the reverse for guest logs)
```

## Clean-room

Only allowed sources ([clean-room.mdc](clean-room.mdc),
[clean-room-third-party-sources.mdc](clean-room-third-party-sources.mdc)).
Forbidden pages still must not be opened or stored.

## When a copy cannot be made

Leave or restore the public citation as soon as a file exists. If the
`output/` original is gone and neither copy exists, tell Ryan which path
failed and note “proof missing” only in the private `manifest.md` (or
private debugging `README.md`)—not as a `capture-log/` path inside the
public spec.
